title: The General Strike
subtitle: The rising lives or dies with the strike.
view-if: crisis_october = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The General Strike

Every plan of the rising begins with a general strike. Without it the hundreds are a few thousand armed men; with it the Reichswehr cannot move its trains, light its barracks or feed its soldiers. But the workers are hungry, the unions are bankrupt, and a strike costs a week's wages that do not exist.

- @railways: Stop the railways first.
- @kitchens: Open strike kitchens in every district.
- @power: Shut down the power stations.

@railways
subtitle: If the trains stop, the army cannot concentrate. The railwaymen must agree.
on-arrival: {!
var ok = Q.worker_support >= 35 || Q.e23_rail_joined == 1;
Q.e23_rail_ok = ok ? 1 : 0;
Q.crisis_momentum += ok ? 8 : 2;
Q.repression += 3;
!}

[? if e23_rail_ok = 1 : The depots of Leipzig, Halle and Berlin-Lichtenberg come out. Troop trains stand in sidings with their engines cold. ?][? if e23_rail_ok = 0 : The railwaymen hesitate. Some trains are stopped by our pickets on the tracks; most run late, but run. ?]

@kitchens
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. The strikers can hold out.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; worker_support += 4; crisis_momentum += 5; unity += 2

The control committees requisition potatoes and flour, and the strike kitchens feed the families in every workers' district.

@power
subtitle: The cities go dark. The strikers' families too.
on-arrival: {!
Q.crisis_momentum += 6;
Q.worker_support -= 2;
Q.militancy += 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

The Klingenberg station goes silent, and with it half of Berlin. The army's searchlights run on its own generators.
